<h2>The science in plain words</h2>
<p>When air cools to its dew point, it can no longer hold all of its water vapour, and the excess turns into liquid. Aqua Tower applies this principle with a heat exchanger and a collection reservoir.</p>
<p>Sensors that track temperature and humidity help you see when conditions suit collection. Collected water then goes through filtration and purification steps covered in the guide.</p>
<p>Warm, humid air gives the best results. Drier air gives less water, so check your local conditions first.</p>
